# Meridian — environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; `.env.example` is not,
# so never put a real key in this file.
#
# These live on the backend only. The published artifact cannot make external
# calls, and anything embedded in app/meridian.html is public to whoever opens
# the page.
#
# STATUS, as of 2026-10-02: nothing in the code reads any of these yet. There
# are no `process.env` reads in backend/ or scripts/ at all. The only mention
# of a key anywhere is a `note: "needs API_DATA_GOV_KEY"` on a Congress.gov
# entry in verify.js that is marked status:"planned". So this file is a record
# of what has been obtained and what the primary-document layer will need —
# not configuration the pipeline currently consumes. A missing key cannot
# break a run today.

# --- Obtained -------------------------------------------------------------

# Google Fact Check Tools API (claims.search).
# Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials.
# No billing account required (confirmed 2026-09-17).
# Key should be API-restricted to Fact Check Tools API only.
GOOGLE_FACTCHECK_KEY=

# --- Free, ~2 minutes each ------------------------------------------------

# One key covers 25 agencies / 450+ APIs: Congress.gov, GovInfo, Regulations.gov.
# Sign up at api.data.gov — issued instantly, no card. Limit 1,000 req/hour.
# This is the only key the code mentions by name (verify.js, Congress.gov,
# status "planned").
API_DATA_GOV_KEY=

# FRED (St. Louis Fed). Account at fredaccount.stlouisfed.org,
# then request at /apikeys. 32-char lowercase string.
# Their terms ask for a distinct key per application — this one is Meridian's.
FRED_API_KEY=

# --- Parked ---------------------------------------------------------------

# data.gov.in — OTP registration blocked (international number).
# Deprioritised: the India sources Meridian actually needs (eGazette, PIB, MEA,
# MHA, RBI) are scrape-tier and need no key. Revisit only if a story turns on
# an Indian statistical dataset.
DATA_GOV_IN_KEY=

# --- Licensed, pending ----------------------------------------------------

# Media Bias/Fact Check. Docs behind an Ad-Free membership (~$3-5/mo);
# data via RapidAPI for research/small projects.
# Rule 11: a displayed MBFC rating must link back to MBFC. The code that would
# enforce that (src/ratings.js) has no importers — see its header.
MBFC_KEY=

# AllSides. Contact form only, no self-serve. Ask about non-commercial
# pricing and whether their ratings cover non-US outlets.
ALLSIDES_KEY=

# --- No key needed --------------------------------------------------------
# GDELT, Bank of Canada Valet, Statistics Canada WDS, Federal Register,
# Eurostat, ECB, EUR-Lex CELLAR, ReliefWeb, World Bank, IMF, OECD, WHO,
# Wikidata, and every RSS feed in config/sources.json.
